{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"12/11/2026 17:41:30","profile":{"player_id":"74623","last_updated":"12/11/2026 17:41","fullname":"Umm-e-Hani","short_display_name":"Umm-e-Hani","name":"Umm-e-Hani","gender":"F","dob":"12/08/1996","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Pakistan","nationality_id":"6","nationality":"Pakistan","nationality_short_code":"PAK","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"2","text":"Bowler","role":"Bowler"},"batting_style":{"id":"1","text":"Right Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"7","text":"Off break"},"writeup":"<p>Sturdy, focused, and armed with an uncomplicated bowling action, Umm-e-Hani is the quintessential modern off-spinner who thrives on precision, relentless discipline, and supreme tactical awareness. Born on August 12, 1996 in Faisalabad, she represents the gritty work ethic typical of cricketers emerging from the industrial heartland of Punjab. Standing tall at the<br />\r\nbowling crease, she extracts steep bounce and sharp drift from a high release point, making her deliveries remarkably awkward for batters to cut or pull. Her calm demeanor and clear head in high-pressure moments have made her a trusted specialist for both regional and national teams.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Her road to the top required immense perseverance, navigating an era where Pakistani women cricket was expanding its player pool. Umm-e-Hani began her competitive journey in 2015, playing for Faisalabad regional teams before representing the Higher Education Commission across national domestic competitions. She spent several seasons refining her arm-ball and perfecting a tight off-stump line in the domestic 50-over and T20 championships. Her ability to operate with an economical run rate and bowl long, probing spells without tiring established her as one of the most reliable finger spinners in the domestic circuit.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Her consistent domestic returns finally bore fruit in late 2022 when she earned her maiden international call-up. Umm-e-Hani made her ODI debut on November 9, 2022 against Ireland at the Gaddafi Stadium in Lahore, immediately showing her capacity to stem the flow of runs in<br />\r\ninternational cricket. In July 2023, she was selected in Pakistan squad for the Asian Games in Hangzhou, China, and shortly after made her T20 debut on September 3, 2023 against South Africa in Karachi. Throughout these matches, she demonstrated an innate understanding of field placements and proved she could execute bowling plans against aggressive international top orders.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>While bowling remained her primary trade, Umm-e-Hani steadily built a reputation as a gritty, capable lower-order batter capable of hanging around with the tail and hitting useful boundaries. During 2024, she was a regular fixture in Pakistan traveling contingents, featuring in the high-profile series against the West Indies at home and the demanding tour of England. Whether bowling in powerplays or choking the scoring during middle overs, she embraced tough assignments with trademark composure, rarely offering free scoring opportunities to opposition batters.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>In 2025, Umm-e-Hani experienced one of the most productive phases of her career in Pakistan domestic tournaments. Leading the spin attack for the Challengers and Invincibles in the Pakistan Women One Day Cup, she regularly tied down opponents and claimed vital breakthroughs, including an impressive three-wicket haul in warm-up fixtures ahead of global qualifiers. Her performances in the National T20 Championship in 2025 underlined her tactical evolution, as she incorporated subtle changes of release angle and flatter seam presentations to thrive on true batting surfaces.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>The year 2026 proved to be an exceptionally busy and successful year for Umm-e-Hani on the international stage. She featured prominently in the bilateral tour of South Africa in early 2026, before playing a crucial role in Pakistan white-ball series against Sri Lanka in July and August<br />\r\n2026, where she snared two wickets for 28 runs in a T20 encounter in Dambulla and bowled full ten-over spells in the ODIs. In September 2026 at the Women Asia Cup T20 in Dubai, she once again played a vital role in restricting opposition totals. At age 30, her seasoned composure and<br />\r\nversatile off-spin make Umm-e-Hani an invaluable anchor in the Pakistan bowling department.</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1130","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Pakistan"},{"id":"2054","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Challengers"},{"id":"2055","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Dynamites"},{"id":"2721","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Pakistan A"},{"id":"2794","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Strikers"},{"id":"3650","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Amazons"},{"id":"3651","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Super"},{"id":"4255","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Multan"}]},"international_debut":{"comp_type_id":"12","comp_type":"ODI International - f","match_id":"211356","match_center":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/tournaments/icc-womens-championship/matches/211356/pakistan-women-vs-ireland-women","series_id":"4752","series_name":"Ireland Women in Pakistan, 3 ODI Series, 2022","match_date":"09/11/2022","for":{"id":"1130","text":"Pakistan","short_name":"PAK"},"vs":{"id":"1125","text":"Ireland","short_name":"IRE"},"venue":{"id":"55","text":"Gaddafi Stadium, Lahore"},"batting":{"runs":"","balls_faced":"","hundreds":"0","innings":[]},"bowling":{"wickets":"1","runs_given":"48","ball_bowled":"60","economy":"4.8","five_wk_hauls":"0","innings":[{"number":"1","wickets":"1","runs_given":"48","ball_bowled":"60","economy":"4.8","five_wk_hauls":"0"}]},"fielding":{"cat